    "description": "PSA International owns and operates container terminals, port infrastructure, and related supply-chain platforms serving global shipping lines and cargo owners. Its operating model is asset-heavy and infrastructure-like, with revenues supported by port handling, terminal operations, and adjacent logistics services across a broad international network. PSA states that its origins date to the Port of Singapore Authority in 1964, while the current PSA International holding structure was formed in 2003 to coordinate global investment and expansion. Public materials describe more than 70 deepsea, rail, and inland terminals in over 180 locations across 45 countries, including North American operations such as PSA Halifax, Penn Terminals, and PSA BDP. In January 2026 PSA reported record 2025 throughput of 105 million TEUs globally, underscoring the scale of the platform within Temasek’s portfolio.",
